# Array.from.call(List, [held], take)
# `this` is not Array, so no declared overload takes the call: it enters the library's function (runtimefunction 48) with its own operands, and the body says what the call does:
# `take` is reached through the body's call of its mapper. Every operand of the call is known, so no code runs that nobody compiles. The same call in the body may also have a callee nobody knows,
# the one of a call that records describe, so what it hands over has escaped: the element.
